Source code for the software compiled into the image

The image is rebuilt every month from the current upstream source of each
component, so it picks up security fixes. Each image records the exact
source it was built from in

    /usr/share/doc/snappier-server/SOURCES

which lists every compiled component with its license, its public
repository or release URL, and the exact commit or release used, plus the
commit of this repository whose Dockerfile configured (and, for Comskip,
patched) it. To read it:

    docker run --rm --entrypoint cat ghcr.io/mackid1993/snappier-server:latest /usr/share/doc/snappier-server/SOURCES

The corresponding source is available from those repositories at those
commits, and from this repository for the build recipe and patch. If a
listed source ever becomes unavailable upstream, open an issue on
github.com/mackid1993/snappier-server and it will be provided.
